- Constructor QuestLog(QuestAsset quest) throws? If null, maybe allow and be inert. Tests can pass null. But AGENTS says validate at boundaries; internal code. Use `ArgumentNullException`? For a MonoBehaviour director, quest might be unassigned; should log error and disable. QuestLog could accept null and be inert for safety; but tests? Simpler: constructor with null allowed, State Inactive, ObjectiveCount 0. `Activate()` returns false if no quest/objectives. This avoids exceptions.
