`GetOrAdd<T>` generic local function with `where T : Component`; local functions with constraints allowed? Yes. Use:
```
T GetOrAdd<T>(GameObject go) where T : Component { var c = go.GetComponent<T>(); return c != null ? c : go.AddComponent<T>(); }
```
- For CapsuleCollider, use GetOrAdd.
- For R13, adding `DialogueSpeaker`/`DialogueMarker` to root. Good.
- For Player, adding `QuestDirector` etc. Good.
- `SerializedObject` helper:
```
void SetRef(Component c, string prop, UnityEngine.Object value) { var so = new SerializedObject(c); var p = so.FindProperty(prop); if (p != null) { p.objectReferenceValue = value; so.ApplyModifiedPropertiesWithoutUndo(); } }
```
But calling multiple `new SerializedObject` and Apply each is okay. Better create one per component and set multiple. Use helper `Apply(Component c, System.Action<SerializedObject> configure)`.
```
void Configure(Component c, System.Action<SerializedObject> action) { var so = new SerializedObject(c); action(so); so.ApplyModifiedPropertiesWithoutUndo(); }
```
- Set array:
```
Configure(director, so => {
  so.FindProperty("_quest").objectReferenceValue = quest;
  ...
  var slotsProp = so.FindProperty("_slots");
  slotsProp.arraySize = slots.Length;
  for (int i=0;i<slots.Length;i++) slotsProp.GetArrayElementAtIndex(i).objectReferenceValue = slots[i];
});
```
- `EditorUtility.SetDirty` for components? `SerializedObject.ApplyModifiedPropertiesWithoutUndo` marks target dirty. Good.
- Scene save `EditorSceneManager.MarkSceneDirty(scene); SaveScene(scene);`.
- Return summary with added components and refs.

