  {
      var names = LoadAll().Select(a => a.name).ToArray();
      foreach (var expected in new[]{"R2_Furnace","R3_Scout","R4_Hauler","R5_Ranger","TrainCompanion_Intro","TrainCompanion_Done"})
          CollectionAssert.Contains(names, expected);
      Assert.GreaterOrEqual(names.Length, 6);
  }
  ```
  This is robust and verifies content. But test count remains 132. Good.
- `AllDialogues_BranchAndReachAnEnd` also checks all nodes have branch; Done will have branch. Good.
- `AllLines_AreRussian` checks every line has Cyrillic; Done lines have Russian; d3 has "R7" and Russian; fine. Intro lines all Russian. Good.
- `AllLines_FitWarningLimit` fine.
- `DialogueFontTests.Font_CoversEveryCharacterUsedByDialogues` will now scan new dialogues and require all characters in font. Our dialogue text includes "ё", "—", "?", maybe font has them (test has them). It might include "R13", digits, Latin; font has ASCII. Good. It may fail on a character like "…" or "«»" not used. We used "—" (em dash) in intro; font test includes "—". Good. We used "ё" in "соберёшь"; font has ё. Fine.
- Need update Done dialogue asset in place. Use execute_code: load asset, find node by id? We have ids node_1..node_4. Set d3 next empty, set action CompleteQuest on d3 and d4. Use `asset.Find("node_3")`, `SetNextId("")`, `SetAction(...)`. Save. Must ensure no duplicate action issues. Both terminals. Good.
- Could also choose to keep d3->d4 and add a new terminal d5 for a second branch. But simpler.
- The user-facing text: d3 "R7 у навеса. Он знает дорогу дальше." then ending; d4 "Иди. Я останусь с грузом." Both complete. The player might miss the "Иди" line if choosing R7, but okay.
- Need update DialogueContentTests. Use Write/Edit.

