#### Thinking

Need to see all roots. Let me get roots names only via execute_code maybe easier. Let's check what execute_code tool expects. Use manage_gameobject? Let's use execute_code with C# to dump hierarchy and positions. Need to know tool name: earlier used "execute_code". Let's call it.

#### Tool: Bash

**Input:**

```json
{
  "command": "UNITY_MCP_PORT=6401 python Tools/Unity/unity_bridge.py call execute_code '{\"code\":\"using UnityEngine; using UnityEditor; using System.Text; public static class Dump { public static string Run() { var sb=new StringBuilder(); foreach(var go in UnityEngine.SceneManagement.SceneManager.GetActiveScene().GetRootGameObjects()){ sb.AppendLine(go.name+\\\" pos=\\\"+go.transform.position.ToString(\\\"F2\\\")+\\\" active=\\\"+go.activeSelf); } return sb.ToString(); } }\"}' 2>&1 | head -60",
