#### Thinking

Interesting R13 in Train has DialogueSpeaker, DialogueMarker, CapsuleCollider but no CharacterController (it stands). We'll replicate in Frontier. Cart has 4 slot children each with CarrySlot component (not shown because only MonoBehaviour on root? Slots are children; earlier QuestDirector references Slot_LB etc). Need Slot component fields and layer. Also Carryable fields.

Let me dump prefab FBX source paths / mesh names and slot components, battery collider sizes, cart collider size, R13 collider, dialogue assets, and Frontier NPC children/bounds.

Also need to know how CarrySlot handles placement and whether cart can be moved after batteries placed (we won't move cart after placing since it arrives already loaded with 4 batteries for DP-01).

Question: In Train, are batteries placed in cart slots in Train scene or on floor? They're on floor as roots, cart at z=10.2. QuestDirector slots reference Slot_* children. Good.

For Frontier DP-01, need cart arrives with four batteries already in slots (already loaded from Train). We can instantiate cart + 4 batteries parented to slots (or just resting on cart) — criterion "тележка оказывается на платформе с четырьмя аккумуляторами". They should be in slots perhaps (Physically carried). Could set each battery as child of slot? CarrySlot has _item field maybe. Let me inspect CarrySlot/Carryable fields and behavior.

Also DP-04: free roam, no blocking. And R7 grants map/scanner once via dialogue actions. Need implement actions GrantScanner/GrantMap. Possibly QuestDirector handles them, but Frontier has no QuestDirector (no quest). Better add a small `EquipmentDirector` or handle in `DialogueController`? DialogueAction already exists with enum values; QuestDirector only handles Accept/Complete. GDD says actions are GrantScanner/GrantMap; implement in a new `PlayerEquipment` component subscribing to DialogueController.ActionInvoked. That is clean: `PlayerEquipment` on Player holds scanner/map flags, subscribes to dialogue actions, grants idempotently.

Where does the dialogue reference come from? Same Player has DialogueController. Add fields `_dialogue`, `_scanner`, `_toast`? Keep toast maybe part of HUD.

Scanner lock: ObjectScanner enabled=false initially in Frontier; PlayerEquipment.GrantScanner enables. But DialogueController disables scanner during dialogue and restores `_scannerWasEnabled` captured at Open. If scanner disabled until grant, dialogue R7 starts with disabled, grant enables during dialogue... then dialogue closes and restores `_scannerWasEnabled=false`, disabling it again. Bug. Need to handle: either grant after dialogue close, or ObjectScanner with `SetAvailable(bool)` separate from `enabled`. Better add availability gate inside ObjectScanner: `_available` default false? But Train also uses scanner — before grant it should be silent in Train too per GDD. So set `_available=false` by default and `Grant()` method. Then no component enable/disable interplay. PlayerEquipment calls scanner.SetAvailable(true). ObjectScanner.LateUpdate/UpdateToggle must bail out if !Available. Also need HUD? ObjectScanner.Views empty -> no labels. Q ignored. 

But then Train scene's scanner currently works; after change it will be silent until grant, which is intended by narrative. Train has no way to grant scanner (R7 in Frontier), so scanner stays silent in Train — matches "До выдачи Q молчит и в поезде, и в депо".

Availability is runtime state per scene; after loading Frontier, default false and grant enables. Later save would persist; but for now okay. If we want it to persist from save later, PlayerEquipment can read save.

Map: flag plus maybe HUD hint? GDD says map is fact in dialogue and scene flag, no minimap. PlayerEquipment.HasMap. Need evidence for acceptance "карта числится выданной". Could expose public bool and maybe PauseMenu journal? No. Tests can verify? EditMode tests can't easily scene-run. We'll verify via Play Mode query.

Maybe include a short one-line toast "КАРТА И СКАНЕР ПОЛУЧЕНЫ" to communicate. UI addition, but minimal and in HUD style. User wants sketches before UI changes. Hmm. We could avoid new UI entirely: after R7 dialogue, QuestTracker? No quest. Could add a line to the pause menu's overview (existing UI) — "СНАРЯЖЕНИЕ: КАРТА, СКАНЕР". That's an existing panel; adding a line is small. But not visible immediately.

I think a subtle HUD toast is appropriate but user preference explicitly says "always show variants before UI decisions". This is not a redesign, just a confirmation line; still UI. To be safe, maybe skip toast and make it visible via scanner actually working (Q + labels) and pause menu equipment line. Actually simplest credible feedback: Q starts working; that's apparent. Map has no visible effect until Stage 3. A pause-journal line "КАРТА: ПОЛУЧЕНА · СКАНЕР: ПОЛУЧЕН" would be good. I'll add equipment status to PauseMenuScreen overview (existing text panel). No new visual design, just a text line. Need to check PauseMenuScreen layout.

Now DP-01 details. We need a cinematic exit. Options:
- Player starts on platform facing train; control locked; R13 walks out of train door with cart following; then control returns.
- Use simple procedural animation, no new animation clips? R13 has Animator with Idle/Walk states. We can set Moving bool via Animator to play Walk while moving. In Train, R13 stands; NpcController could drive R13 if we give CharacterController. But NpcController's route loops; we need one-shot. Could write `DepotArrivalDirector` that moves R13/cart transforms with Animator Moving bool. No physics needed for R13 (it has CapsuleCollider static). Move transform directly in coroutine; cart move transform too.

But better use NpcController waypoints? It loops and random pauses, not one-shot. For a scripted exit, custom coroutine is fine and deterministic.

Cart is heavy; "за ним выезжает тележка" implies cart follows. We can animate both along a path from train door to platform; R13 walks, cart follows behind at offset. Need door open: DepotTrain is decorative closed train; no door. Hmm. We can fake by starting R13/cart just at the train side (x=-7.4) as if emerging from between cars, and put a "DepotDoor" object? DP-01 explicitly "Дверь вагона открыта". The decorative train may have doors modeled? Let me inspect DepotTrain bounds and children, maybe car models have doors but not pivot. Could add an open doorway gap by moving a door child if exists? Let me check FBX hierarchy for DepotTrain children deeper.

Let's dump all descendants of DepotTrain in Frontier. Currently Train loaded. Load Frontier and dump. Or inspect prefab MenuFreightTrain? The DepotTrain children: TrainCarA/B/Loco. Could be one FBX. Open Frontier and dump hierarchy depth + renderer bounds.

