#### Thinking

Frontier train: bounds center z=-3.9, size z 23.89, so spans z -15.8 to 7.95, x -9.33 to -6.67. Platform x -15..15, z -7..7, top y=0.6. Player pos y .7 (character controller pivot) on platform? Player starts z=-6 (platform edge). Train is left of platform x -8 but spans z range. Door side at x=-6.67; platform extends to x=-15 (under train? platform too wide, extends beneath train). Fine. Characters at y=.7 stand on platform? Platform top y=0.6; character pivot at 0.7 => feet at 0.6.

Train bounds y 0..3.8. Door would be around z? Cars along z. We could pick door position near z=-2 or z=2. There's no doorway modeled; but we can fake: R13 and cart start beside the train at x=-6.2 (just outside train side) and walk onto platform. To satisfy "дверь открыта", maybe not model it. Could add a dark "open door" panel on train side? Without modifying FBX, add a black quad/door frame at x=-6.65, z=... Aligned to train side. But a fake door is cosmetic.

Alternative: R13 starts behind the train car (x=-9.5) and walks around the end? Less good.

Maybe simplest: place a doorway "cutout" illusion: a dark vertical rectangle with emissive cyan trim on train side, plus R13 emerges from x=-6.75 at that z. The player sees the glow and them stepping out. This is reasonable for placeholder.

Need a cart to "выехать" behind R13. We can animate R13 from x=-6.7 to x=-3.2 along +x, then turn to z maybe. Cart follows 2m behind along same path, then settles parallel. But cart width 2.4 x 1.9; okay on platform.

We need batteries in cart. Instantiate 4 Prop_Battery at slot positions as children of cart slots? In Train they are separate root and placed by player. In Frontier they should sit on the cart from the start, so place them at slot world positions (or parent to slots with local zero). A Carryable battery in a slot: CarrySlot likely has Placed event when item placed. If we want them "already placed", just position them at slot positions without marking slots occupied (slots' _item null). Future Stage 3 unload quest would need slots marked; but not now. However the carry system's slot detection checks nearest slot; an unparented battery at slot may be pickable. Not a problem. But "4 batteries on cart" visually should be children of cart so they move with it during arrival. If parented to slot transforms, they move with cart. But then CarryController pickup would unparent? Let's inspect Carryable/CarrySlot to see parenting behavior.

