#### Thinking

Good. Now Frontier needs R13 arrival dialogue? DP-01 is scripted exit; maybe R13 after exit says something? GDD DP-01 doesn't require dialogue; R13 and cart exit. Could add optional R13 line? Not needed. R13 stays with cart; player free to talk? Not specified. Keep no speaker or speaker with a short line? GDD says R7 is the greeter. Adding an R13 dialogue would be extra scope. Skip.

DP-02: two guards: R16_Warden at train exit (already A at -4,2) and R8_Bulwark at gate exit to road. Currently no R8_Bulwark; there's gate at (12,0,10) (rotated, bounds x 6-13). Need add R8_Bulwark at gate, from prefab Robot R8. Add ScanTarget, DialogueSpeaker with short 2-3 line warning dialogue, and collider. R16 A/B: GDD says "R16_Warden у выхода из поезда и R8_Bulwark у выезда из депо к дороге." There are two R16 currently; one should be replaced by R8? GDD says "В депо выходят R13 и тележка, стоят два R16" in acceptance criteria (§ "Критерии готово"), but DP-02 says R16 at train exit and R8 at gate. Hmm inconsistency: acceptance says два R16. Maybe two R16 plus R8? "стоят два R16" could be the two guards; DP-02 specifically names R16 and R8. Let's follow DP-02: R16_Warden at train exit (existing A), R8_Bulwark at gate; keep R16_B as a second warden? Extra guard doesn't hurt, but acceptance says two R16. We could keep both R16s plus add R8 = 3 guards. DP-02 only requires both visible and talkable. Existing A at (-4,2) near train; B at (4,-3) mid-platform. Add R8 at gate (9,0,10 near road). Might be crowded but fine.

Better: repurpose B as R8_Bulwark? Then two R16 becomes one. I'd rather add R8 near gate and keep two R16 (matches "два R16" acceptance). But then DP-02 "R16 у выхода из поезда и R8 у выезда" satisfied. Extra R16_B is flavor. Fine.

Each guard needs a short warning dialogue on E. Use DialogueScreen Russian. Name from ScanTarget: "R16 WARDEN" category "GUARD"? ScanTarget category could be "ОХРАНА"? Scanner labels are Latin-only per ScanTarget doc (font LiberationSans SDF has no Cyrillic). But HUD may use Cyrillic font now? PlayerHud/ScanLabelView check. Scan labels use Latin atlas. Keep display names/categories Latin: "R16 WARDEN", "GUARD"; dialogue screen uses Cyrillic font and DisplayName from ScanTarget (Latin, okay as names). Good.

R7 grants map/scanner: dialogue 4-6 nodes, node with GrantScanner and node with GrantMap (idempotent). Could both actions on different nodes. PlayerEquipment listens; grant idempotent. Repeat dialogue doesn't regrant (flags stay, no duplicate effect). "новых целей нет" — no quest.

Need scanner available gate. Add `_available` to ObjectScanner default false? But Game scene uses scanner; would become unavailable unless granted (no grant there). Game scene is out of flow (legacy), but existing behavior shouldn't break? AGENTS says Game is outside flow. We could default `_available = true` and in Frontier set false via serialized field, with `PlayerEquipment` granting. But GDD says Q silent in Train too. Train should be set false as well. Better default true for backwards compatibility, then set false in Train and Frontier scenes. But new scenes/other scenes (Game) keep working. Serialized `_available` initial true. Hmm naming: `_granted`/`_availableAtStart`. Set `_available = true` in Awake from serialized? Provide `[SerializeField] private bool _available = true;` and `public bool Available`. `Grant()` sets true. `SetAvailable(false)` on scene init (serialized false in Train/Frontier). LateUpdate: if !Available, clear views? On disable-like behavior. Add early return and clear state once when availability false. Actually if we set serialized false, LateUpdate early returns; Views empty; Q ignored. Pause menu toggling enabled harmless.

PlayerEquipment:
- fields: `_dialogue`, `_scanner`, `_pause`? For HUD line, add `HasScanner`, `HasMap`, event `Changed` so PauseMenu can display.
- OnEnable subscribe DialogueController.ActionInvoked.
- On action GrantScanner -> `_scanner.Grant()`; HasScanner=true. GrantMap -> HasMap=true.
- Idempotent naturally.
- Maybe auto-grant by default? no.

PauseMenu overview equipment line: add `_equipment` field and in BuildQuestText append "\n\nСНАРЯЖЕНИЕ: КАРТА — ... · СКАНЕР — ...". But BuildQuestText early returns when no quest; need equipment line there too. Frontier has QuestDirector null, so overview says "Активных заданий нет. Подойдите к R13 и нажмите E." — wrong for Frontier. We should improve: if equipment assigned, append line. Also the hint "Подойдите к R13" is Train-specific and wrong in Frontier. Could change general text to "Активных заданий нет." and quest hint only when _questDirector exists. Hmm, in Frontier _questDirector null. Use "Активных заданий нет.\n\nОсмотритесь." Fine.

Now the arrival sequence. Need `DepotArrivalDirector`:
- fields: `_locomotion`, `_rig`, `_r13` Transform, `_cart` Transform, `_player` Transform?, `_door` maybe, `_duration`, `_startDelay`.
- On Start: lock locomotion, pause camera (SetPaused? that freezes camera view entirely and hides cursor? SetPaused(true) likely pauses rig updates but keeps cursor? Dialogue uses it). Better `SetCinematic(true)` which pauses rig updates but keeps cursor hidden, like finale. But SetCinematic doesn't allow look? It should freeze. DP-01 says player gets control after; during 5s watch, freeze input. Use `_locomotion.SetConversationLock(true)` and `_rig.SetCinematic(true)`.
- Optionally move camera? A short pan from door to cart would be cinematic. But camera is player-attached orbit. We could leave camera on player. Player starts at (0,0.7,-6) facing train? yaw 0 looks +z, train at left x=-8. Not ideal. Set player start at (0,0.7,2) and rotation facing -x (yaw 270)? Camera follows. Hmm.

Let's design arrival placement:
- Train door at x≈-6.5, z≈2.0 (between cars). Platform top y=0.6; actors pivot y=0.7.
- R13 starts at (-7.2, 0.7, 2.0) hidden inside/at door, moves to (-3.2, 0.7, 2.0) over 3s, facing +x (rotation y=90).
- Cart starts at (-7.4, 0.6?, 2.0) behind R13, follows to (-1.0, 0.6, 2.0)? Cart scale: prefab from FBX at scale 1; in Train cart at y=0 sits on floor (train floor y=0). Cart height 1.9? bounds 2.4x1.9x1.15. On frontier platform top 0.6 => cart y=0.6. It should be behind R13: R13 final (-2.5, 0.7, 2), cart final (-0.2, 0.6, 2). Player at (2.5, 0.7, -2)? Player watches from front-right. Awning posts at x±10, z -2/5; fine.

But R16_A at (-4,0.7,2) blocks path. Move R16_A to (-4,0.7,4.5) near train but off the path; or make R13 path z=0.5. Let's set path z=0.5. R16_A at (-4, 0.7, 2.5) still near. Cart width 1.9 in z? Rotated? Cart default rotation in Train 0: bounds x 2.4, z 1.15. So path along +x works; cart width in z 1.15. R13 final (-2.6, 0.7, 0.5), cart final (-0.2, 0.6, 0.5). Player start at (2.2, 0.7, -2.5) looking toward -x? yaw 270 faces -x. Camera orbit yaw default? PlayerCameraRig uses player yaw maybe. We can set Player rotation y=270 (faces -x). Then sees R13/cart coming from left-front? Player at x=2.2 looking -x toward door at -7. Cart stops at x=-0.2, close to player. Maybe player should be farther: (4.5, 0.7, -2.5), facing -x. Umbrella covers 22x9 centered z=1.5 (z -3..6). Fine.

Camera's initial position in Frontier (0,2.3,-7.5) won't match player after we move player; Camera rig will follow on Awake. Fine.

Player starts outside control during sequence. `_rig.SetCinematic(true)` stops rig update; camera may stay at old position. Better don't freeze camera; just lock locomotion and hide? If rig updates normally, camera snaps behind player at start. Then sequence plays; player can look around with mouse but can't move. That's fine and gives player agency. Use `_locomotion.SetConversationLock(true)` only. But the initial snap: camera at 0,2.3,-7.5 while player at 4.5 -> camera flies over first frames? Rig likely computes desired instantly. Acceptable.

Maybe add a short camera pan? Not necessary.

- Animator: R13 root Animator with controller; set bool "Moving" true during move. Check controller param exists. Probably "Moving" like Npc. Use Animator.StringToHash("Moving"). R13's Animator might have Idle only? Train R13 stands and DialogueSpeaker; check controller states. Probably R13_Prospector_Model controller has Idle/Walk. Let's inspect controller parameters/clips.

- Cart: no animation; move transform. Add a subtle hover bob? It's a grav cart; maybe bob. Keep simple, move smoothly.

- Door: add an "open door" visual. Maybe not needed; but train is closed. Could place a dark doorway at x=-6.62 (side), z=0.5, y=1.1, size 0.05x2.2x1.2 (plane) plus cyan edge strips. That's 3D level geometry via primitives with standard material. But user's style is minimal; a dark opening with a faint cyan frame reads as open door. We can create a quad (Cube thin) with dark material and two thin cyan emissive edges. We need materials. Existing level uses materials; we can reuse an existing dark material from scene (e.g., DepotPlatform material) and a cyan material? Let's check existing materials in Content/Materials. Maybe `Level_Cyan` exists. List.

Also cart in DP-01 should end on platform with 4 batteries; we can instantiate the cart and 4 batteries as children of slots with Carryable disabled? If parented to slot with batteries, Carryable.Awake records home at runtime (position at slot) and colliders enabled; but Carryable.IsPlaced false; collider would collide with cart (and player). In Train batteries have colliders enabled when on floor. On cart slots, in Train placing calls Place -> colliders disabled. For arrival, call `Place` requires IsCarried true then sets parent; could call `Take(anchor)` then `Place(slot)` during setup, resulting IsPlaced=true and colliders off; visual child. But then CarrySlot.Occupant should be set; TryPlace triggers Placed event. We can set slot.Occupant via TryPlace after Take. But at edit-time we can't call runtime methods (Awake not run) meaningfully (could via execute_code in edit mode, but values are runtime-only, not serialized). At runtime, after scene loads, DepotArrivalDirector can mark them placed. Simpler: just place battery objects as children of slot transforms in the scene, with Carryable components but colliders disabled in the prefab instance? Disabling collider at edit time is serialized. But IsPlaced remains false, so CarryController could pick them up. That's actually okay/fun: player can unload the cart. DP-01 only requires cart with 4 batteries. Stage 3 will require unloading. Allowing pickup now is not harmful. But quest gating? RequiredQuestId empty -> carryable anytime. Fine.

But when cart moves during arrival, batteries are children of cart slots, so they move. Parenting battery under slot with localPosition zero aligns pivot at slot; battery pivot? In Train battery pivot at bottom center (we fixed pivot), slot y=0.55 is above cart floor; battery pivot bottom at 0.55 means it floats 0.55 above cart? In Train, slot world y=0.55 and battery placed there has pivot at slot => battery bottom at 0.55, maybe the slot is the top surface? Cart base height maybe 0.55. Good.

Battery scale? In Train roots at y=0, so pivot bottom at floor. Cart slot y=0.55, so bottom at 0.55, correct on cart bed.

Collider: battery BoxCollider enabled; on cart, could collide with player; fine. But it also might collide with cart's BoxCollider? Static-ish; no Rigidbody so no physics push, just blocking. Player can't reach the cart bed? BoxCollider cart blocks. Fine.

