#### Thinking

R13 was not in active scene (Frontier loaded), so no capsule. Open Train to dump R13 capsule? We saw earlier Train R13 has CapsuleCollider; need settings. Let's load Train, dump collider, then back to Frontier. Also player controller dims. Use one script that loads Train? SceneManager.LoadScene in edit mode not allowed. Use EditorSceneManager.OpenScene.

Alternatively use prefab R13 doesn't include collider. We'll pick capsule center (0,1.0,0), radius 0.35, height 1.9. Standard. R13 visual bounds 1.16x2.09x1.13 (wide robot); capsule 0.4 radius, height 1.9 center y=0.95. Fine.

Battery bounds: (0.98, 0.95, 0.70) — width x, height 0.95, depth 0.70. In Train rotated 90 around Y => footprint x 0.70, z 0.98. Slots separated 1.1 in x and 0.8 in z: rotated 90 gives depth 0.98 > 0.8 overlap in z. Hmm. If unrotated, x 0.98 < 1.1 and z 0.70 < 0.8, fits! So on the cart, batteries should be rotation identity (not 90) to fit the four slots. In Train floor they're rotated 90 for a neat row along z. For slots, Place sets localRotation identity, so they'd be unrotated and fit. Good.

Cart bounds 2.40 x 1.15 x 1.89 (x, y, z). Slot positions ±0.55 x, ±0.4 z. Battery unrotated footprint 0.98 x 0.70; gaps 0.12 and 0.1. Good.

Cart height 1.15; R13 2.09 tall; visible behind cart. Great.

Wait GDD said cart 2.4×1.9×1.15 (maybe length×width×height); actual bounds 2.4 (x), 1.15 (y height), 1.89 (z). Fine.

Now, R13 movement animation: Moving bool; controller has Idle/Walk. Set animator speed? NpcController adjusts; for scripted move, we can set Moving=true, speed = distance/duration / clip speed? If unknown clip speed ~1.0; set animator.speed=1. Walk at ~3.2m over 3.2s = 1 m/s, close to walk clip 0.9. Fine.

Cart is 2.4 long in x, moving along +x; door width 3.2 in z. Good.

Battery placement at runtime: Director calls `Take(slot.transform)` then `slot.TryPlace(battery)`. Take reparents and zeroes local pos, then Place same. Works. But Carryable.Awake caches homePosition at spawn. Batteries spawn as children of slots? If we instantiate batteries as scene roots at their slot positions, then at Awake home = slot world pos; later cart moves, batteries stay (not children until Director places them). Director should run after Awake of batteries; other components' Awake order unspecified. If Director's Awake runs before battery Awake, then Take/Place parents them and sets positions; battery Awake then records home = current (slot) position, colliders. Fine. If after, home = spawn slot pos. Either way. Make Director Start (not Awake) to ensure all Awakes done. Fine.

Batteries: instantiate at slot world positions with rotation identity. We need slot world positions computed from cart transform at build time. We can create batteries as children of slots in edit mode, which is simpler, but then `Take` home etc. Director still places. Parent them to slot with local zero. Then they move with cart even before Director runs. Good. But Carryable.Awake home = world position at scene start (cart start). If placed, no drop. Fine. Parent battery to slot and local zero in edit mode; component colliders enabled by default -> colliding with cart static. No Rigidbody, so okay. Director then Place disables colliders. 

Cart slots need CarrySlot components; Director references them. Fine.

Now player start and camera. Let me check PlayerCameraRig for how it initializes and whether SetCinematic vs SetPaused hides cursor.

