But the exterior body's **lower wall** starts at z=0 (floor), while the train root y=1.0; the body bottom at 1.0 (floor); the platform 0.6. The lower wall (brown) begins at 1.0, so the train's **underside** (underframe) is between 0.56 and 1.0, visible above platform? The platform edge at x=-4; underframe x -11.7..-4.3, outside platform; wheels at x -10.95..-5.05. Fine. The door threshold 1.0; R13 steps down 0.4.

